        "type": "tool_result",
        "content": "     1→[\n     2→  {\n     3→    \"title\": \"Show HN: Libretto – Making AI browser automations deterministic\",\n     4→    \"description\": \"A developer showcased Libretto, a tool for making AI browser automations deterministic, addressing reliability challenges in AI-powered web automation and testing workflows.\",\n     5→    \"author\": \"muchael\",\n     6→    \"source\": \"HN\",\n     7→    \"url\": \"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40385234\",\n     8→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-16\",\n     9→    \"topics\": [\"browser automation\", \"deterministic AI\", \"testing\", \"developer tools\"],\n    10→    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n    11→  },\n    12→  {\n    13→    \"title\": \"Ask HN: Who is using OpenClaw?\",\n    14→    \"description\": \"Hacker News discussion asking about real-world adoption and use cases for OpenClaw, revealing community interest and practical applications of autonomous AI agents in development workflows.\",\n    15→    \"author\": \"misterchocolat\",\n    16→    \"source\": \"HN\",\n    17→    \"url\": \"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40386541\",\n    18→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-16\",\n    19→    \"topics\": [\"OpenClaw\", \"adoption\", \"developer tools\", \"AI agents\"],\n    20→    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n    21→  },\n    22→  {\n    23→    \"title\": \"Gemini 3.1 Flash TTS - Google's new text-to-speech model with prompt-based voice control\",\n    24→    \"description\": \"Google released Gemini 3.1 Flash TTS, a text-to-speech model that can be directed using detailed prompts. The prompting guide is surprisingly detailed, allowing control over accent, style, dynamics, pace, and even specific recording scenarios. Simon Willison tested it with different regional accents (Brixton, Newcastle, Exeter) and noted the results. He also used Gemini 3.1 Pro to 'vibe code' a UI for trying out the TTS functionality.\",\n    25→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    26→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    27→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/15/gemini-flash-tts/\",\n    28→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-15\",\n    29→    \"topics\": [\"text-to-speech\", \"google\", \"gemini\", \"prompt-engineering\", \"generative-ai\", \"llms\", \"vibe-coding\"],\n    30→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    31→  },\n    32→  {\n    33→    \"title\": \"Anthropic's rise is giving some OpenAI investors second thoughts\",\n    34→    \"description\": \"Investment analysis suggesting Anthropic's momentum is causing OpenAI investors to reconsider their positions, highlighting growing competition in the AI space and shifting market dynamics.\",\n    35→    \"author\": \"Connie Loizos\",\n    36→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n    37→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/15/anthropics-rise-giving-openai-investors-second-thoughts/\",\n    38→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-15\",\n    39→    \"topics\": [\"Anthropic\", \"OpenAI\", \"investment\", \"market competition\"],\n    40→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n    41→  },\n    42→  {\n    43→    \"title\": \"Anthropic co-founder confirms the company briefed the Trump administration on Mythos\",\n    44→    \"description\": \"Anthropic co-founder confirmed briefing the Trump administration on Mythos, indicating growing government interest in AI capabilities and potential regulatory engagement.\",\n    45→    \"author\": \"Sarah Perez\",\n    46→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n    47→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/15/anthropic-trump-administration-mythos-briefing/\",\n    48→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-15\",\n    49→    \"topics\": [\"Anthropic\", \"Mythos\", \"government\", \"policy\", \"regulation\"],\n    50→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    51→  },\n    52→  {\n    53→    \"title\": \"Google adds AI Skills to Chrome to help you save favorite workflows\",\n    54→    \"description\": \"Google introduced AI Skills in Chrome, allowing users to save AI prompts as repeatable workflows. This feature enables automation of common tasks and integration of AI assistance directly into the browser.\",\n    55→    \"author\": \"Sarah Perez\",\n    56→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n    57→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/15/google-chrome-ai-skills-feature/\",\n    58→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-15\",\n    59→    \"topics\": [\"Google\", \"Chrome\", \"AI workflows\", \"browser automation\", \"productivity\"],\n    60→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    61→  },\n    62→  {\n    63→    \"title\": \"Google launches a Gemini AI app on Mac\",\n    64→    \"description\": \"Google released a Gemini app for macOS, allowing users to access Gemini from anywhere on their desktop and share windows. This marks Google's continued push to make Gemini more accessible across platforms.\",\n    65→    \"author\": \"Emma Roth\",\n    66→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n    67→    \"url\": \"https://www.theverge.com/2026/4/14/24138473/google-gemini-mac-app\",\n    68→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-14\",\n    69→    \"topics\": [\"Google Gemini\", \"macOS\", \"AI apps\", \"cross-platform\"],\n    70→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    71→  },\n    72→  {\n    73→    \"title\": \"Adobe embraces conversational AI editing, marking a 'fundamental shift' in creative work\",\n    74→    \"description\": \"Adobe announced new conversational AI editing capabilities in Firefly, representing what they call a 'fundamental shift' in how creative professionals interact with AI tools for content creation.\",\n    75→    \"author\": \"Jess Weatherbed\",\n    76→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n    77→    \"url\": \"https://www.theverge.com/2026/4/14/24137884/adobe-firefly-conversational-ai-editing\",\n    78→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-14\",\n    79→    \"topics\": [\"Adobe\", \"conversational AI\", \"creative tools\", \"Firefly\"],\n    80→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    81→  },\n    82→  {\n    83→    \"title\": \"Claude Code redesign focuses on managing multiple AI agents\",\n    84→    \"description\": \"Anthropic redesigned the Claude Code desktop app with new features for managing multiple AI agents simultaneously, including a sidebar for managing sessions, drag-and-drop workspace customization, and built-in terminal and file editor.\",\n    85→    \"author\": \"Stevie Bonifield\",\n    86→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n    87→    \"url\": \"https://www.theverge.com/2026/4/14/24137500/claude-code-redesign-multiple-ai-agents\",\n    88→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-14\",\n    89→    \"topics\": [\"Claude Code\", \"Anthropic\", \"multi-agent systems\", \"developer tools\"],\n    90→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    91→  },\n    92→  {\n    93→    \"title\": \"Gemini with Personal Intelligence is rolling out in more regions\",\n    94→    \"description\": \"Google's Personal Intelligence feature, which allows Gemini to access information from Gmail, Google Photos, Search, and YouTube watch history, is now rolling out globally (excluding UK, Switzerland, and EEA), starting with paid subscribers.\",\n    95→    \"author\": \"Emma Roth\",\n    96→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n    97→    \"url\": \"https://www.theverge.com/2026/4/14/24137685/gemini-personal-intelligence-global-rollout\",\n    98→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-14\",\n    99→    \"topics\": [\"Google Gemini\", \"Personal Intelligence\", \"privacy\", \"data access\"],\n   100→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   101→  },\n   102→  {\n   103→    \"title\": \"Microsoft says its latest AI image model is a 'production workhorse'\",\n   104→    \"description\": \"Microsoft debuted MAI-Image-2-Efficient on Microsoft Foundry and MAI Playground, describing it as a faster, cheaper 'production workhorse' for businesses needing volume, speed, and cost control for product shots, marketing creatives, and UI mockups.\",\n   105→    \"author\": \"Tom Warren\",\n   106→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n   107→    \"url\": \"https://www.theverge.com/2026/4/14/24137186/microsoft-mai-image-2-efficient\",\n   108→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-14\",\n   109→    \"topics\": [\"Microsoft\", \"AI image generation\", \"enterprise\", \"cost efficiency\"],\n   110→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   111→  },\n   112→  {\n   113→    \"title\": \"Datasette CSRF protection modernization - Moving from tokens to Sec-Fetch-Site headers\",\n   114→    \"description\": \"Simon Willison landed a PR to replace Datasette's token-based CSRF protection with a modern approach using Sec-Fetch-Site headers, inspired by Go 1.25 and Filippo Valsorda's research. This removes the need for scattered CSRF tokens in templates and eliminates the skip_csrf plugin hook. Notably, Claude Code did much of the work across 10 commits, but Simon decided to write PR descriptions by hand to maintain honesty and conciseness.\",\n   115→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   116→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   117→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/14/csrf/\",\n   118→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-14\",\n   119→    \"topics\": [\"csrf\", \"security\", \"datasette\", \"ai-assisted-programming\"],\n   120→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   121→  },\n   122→  {\n   123→    \"title\": \"OpenAI's GPT-5.4-Cyber model and Trusted Access program\",\n   124→    \"description\": \"OpenAI announced GPT-5.4-Cyber, a 'cyber-permissive' variant fine-tuned for defensive cybersecurity use cases, along with their Trusted Access for Cyber program that allows users to verify identity via government ID to gain reduced friction access. Simon notes this appears to be OpenAI's answer to Anthropic's Claude Mythos and Project Glasswing. The announcement emphasizes OpenAI's years of cybersecurity work and goals to democratize access.\",\n   125→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   126→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   127→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/14/openai-cyber/\",\n   128→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-14\",\n   129→    \"topics\": [\"security\", \"ai\", \"openai\", \"generative-ai\", \"llms\", \"anthropic\", \"ai-security-research\"],\n   130→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   131→  },\n   132→  {\n   133→    \"title\": \"Cybersecurity as Proof of Work - The economic implications of AI security testing\",\n   134→    \"description\": \"The UK's AI Safety Institute published an evaluation of Claude Mythos Preview's cyber capabilities. Drew Breunig notes that the more tokens (money) spent, the better the security results, leading to a concerning equation: 'to harden a system you need to spend more tokens discovering exploits than attackers will spend exploiting them.' This makes open source libraries more valuable since security tokens spent on them can be shared across all users.\",\n   135→    \"author\": \"Drew Breunig (covered by Simon Willison)\",\n   136→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   137→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/14/cyber-proof-of-work/\",\n   138→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-14\",\n   139→    \"topics\": [\"open-source\", \"ai\", \"generative-ai\", \"llms\", \"vibe-coding\", \"ai-security-research\"],\n   140→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n   141→  },\n   142→  {\n   143→    \"title\": \"Google brings its Gemini Personal Intelligence feature to India\",\n   144→    \"description\": \"Google expanded Gemini Personal Intelligence to India, allowing the AI to access personal data from Gmail, Photos, Search, and YouTube to provide more contextualized assistance.\",\n   145→    \"author\": \"Ivan Mehta\",\n   146→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n   147→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/14/google-gemini-personal-intelligence-india/\",\n   148→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-14\",\n   149→    \"topics\": [\"Google\", \"Gemini\", \"Personal Intelligence\", \"India\", \"data access\"],\n   150→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   151→  },\n   152→  {\n   153→    \"title\": \"Microsoft is working on yet another OpenClaw-like agent\",\n   154→    \"description\": \"Microsoft continues developing OpenClaw-like AI agents, signaling sustained investment in autonomous AI systems that can perform complex multi-step tasks with minimal human intervention.\",\n   155→    \"author\": \"Julie Bort\",\n   156→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n   157→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/14/microsoft-openclaw-like-agent-development/\",\n   158→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-14\",\n   159→    \"topics\": [\"Microsoft\", \"OpenClaw\", \"AI agents\", \"autonomous systems\"],\n   160→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   161→  },\n   162→  {\n   163→    \"title\": \"Microsoft is testing OpenClaw-like AI bots for Copilot\",\n   164→    \"description\": \"Microsoft is developing OpenClaw-like AI agents for its Copilot platform, continuing the trend of major tech companies building autonomous AI agents that can perform complex tasks.\",\n   165→    \"author\": \"The Verge Staff\",\n   166→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n   167→    \"url\": \"https://www.theverge.com/2026/4/13/24135530/microsoft-copilot-openclaw-like-ai-bots\",\n   168→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-13\",\n   169→    \"topics\": [\"Microsoft\", \"Copilot\", \"OpenClaw\", \"AI agents\"],\n   170→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   171→  },\n   172→  {\n   173→    \"title\": \"SoftBank creates new company building 'physical AI'\",\n   174→    \"description\": \"SoftBank announced a new initiative to build AI models that can autonomously control machines and robots by 2030, with buy-in from Sony, Honda, and Nippon Steel. This represents a major push into 'physical AI' for robotics and autonomous systems.\",\n   175→    \"author\": \"Robert Hart\",\n   176→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n   177→    \"url\": \"https://www.theverge.com/2026/4/13/24135045/softbank-physical-ai-robots\",\n   178→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-13\",\n   179→    \"topics\": [\"SoftBank\", \"physical AI\", \"robotics\", \"autonomous systems\"],\n   180→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   181→  },\n   182→  {\n   183→    \"title\": \"Vercel CEO Guillermo Rauch signals IPO readiness as AI agents fuel revenue surge\",\n   184→    \"description\": \"Vercel's CEO indicated the company is preparing for an IPO, driven by significant revenue growth from AI agent adoption. This highlights the commercial success and market demand for AI-powered developer tools.\",\n   185→    \"author\": \"Marina Temkin\",\n   186→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n   187→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/13/vercel-ceo-guillermo-rauch-ipo-ai-agents-revenue/\",\n   188→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-13\",\n   189→    \"topics\": [\"Vercel\", \"IPO\", \"AI agents\", \"developer tools\", \"business\"],\n   190→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n   191→  },\n   192→  {\n   193→    \"title\": \"Steve Yegge vs Google on AI adoption - Industry-wide 20/20/60 adoption curve\",\n   194→    \"description\": \"Steve Yegge claimed Google engineering has the same AI adoption footprint as John Deere (20% agentic power users, 20% refusers, 60% using chat tools). Google's Addy Osmani and Demis Hassabis strongly disputed this, noting over 40K SWEs use agentic coding weekly with access to internal tools. The debate highlights internal AI adoption challenges across the industry and the 18-month hiring freeze that may have prevented fresh perspectives.\",\n   195→    \"author\": \"Steve Yegge, Addy Osmani, Demis Hassabis\",\n   196→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   197→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/13/google-ai/\",\n   198→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-13\",\n   199→    \"topics\": [\"google\", \"generative-ai\", \"agentic-engineering\", \"ai\", \"llms\"],\n   200→    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n   201→  },\n   202→  {\n   203→    \"title\": \"Exploring the new Servo crate - Embeddable browser engine for Rust\",\n   204→    \"description\": \"Following the April 2026 release of the servo v0.1.0 crate, Simon used Claude Code to explore what the embeddable browser engine can do. He built a CLI tool called 'servo-shot' for taking screenshots of URLs, which successfully rendered the Hacker News homepage. While compiling Servo to WebAssembly isn't feasible due to heavy thread usage, Claude built a playground for html5ever and markup5ever_rcdom crates.\",\n   205→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   206→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   207→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/13/servo-crate/\",\n   208→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-13\",\n   209→    \"topics\": [\"research\", \"browsers\", \"rust\", \"webassembly\", \"claude-code\", \"servo\"],\n   210→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   211→  },\n   212→  {\n   213→    \"title\": \"The peril of laziness lost - How LLMs lack the virtue of laziness\",\n   214→    \"description\": \"Bryan Cantrill argues that LLMs inherently lack the virtue of laziness - work costs nothing to an LLM, so they don't optimize for future time and will happily add layers of complexity. This highlights how essential human laziness is: our finite time forces us to develop crisp abstractions because we don't want to waste time dealing with clunky systems. Left unchecked, LLMs make systems larger, not better.\",\n   215→    \"author\": \"Bryan Cantrill (covered by Simon Willison)\",\n   216→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   217→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/13/laziness/\",\n   218→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-13\",\n   219→    \"topics\": [\"bryan-cantrill\", \"ai\", \"llms\", \"ai-assisted-programming\", \"generative-ai\"],\n   220→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n   221→  },\n   222→  {\n   223→    \"title\": \"The AI code wars are heating up\",\n   224→    \"description\": \"Analysis of how OpenAI, Google, and Anthropic are intensifying competition in AI-powered coding tools, with each major player vying for dominance in developer workflows and AI-assisted programming.\",\n   225→    \"author\": \"David Pierce\",\n   226→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n   227→    \"url\": \"https://www.theverge.com/2026/4/12/24132398/ai-code-wars-openai-google-anthropic\",\n   228→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-12\",\n   229→    \"topics\": [\"AI coding\", \"developer tools\", \"market competition\", \"OpenAI\", \"Google\", \"Anthropic\"],\n   230→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n   231→  },\n   232→  {\n   233→    \"title\": \"Audio transcription with Gemma 4 E2B using MLX\",\n   234→    \"description\": \"Simon shared a recipe for transcribing audio files on macOS using the 10.28 GB Gemma 4 E2B model with MLX and mlx-vlm. The 'uv run' command makes it easy to run transcription with various models. He tested it on a 14-second WAV file and found it worked well, with minor transcription errors due to audio quality.\",\n   235→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   236→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   237→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/12/gemma-transcription/\",\n   238→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-12\",\n   239→    \"topics\": [\"uv\", \"mlx\", \"ai\", \"gemma\", \"llms\", \"speech-to-text\", \"python\", \"generative-ai\"],\n   240→    \"type\": \"tutorial\"\n   241→  },\n   242→  {\n   243→    \"title\": \"OpenAI responds to Axios HTTP hack by updating security certificates\",\n   244→    \"description\": \"After hackers compromised an Axios maintainer account and inserted malicious code affecting ChatGPT's macOS apps, OpenAI issued updates and new security certificates to mitigate risks to Windows, macOS, and Linux users.\",\n   245→    \"author\": \"Terrence O'Brien\",\n   246→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n   247→    \"url\": \"https://www.theverge.com/2026/4/11/24128930/openai-axios-http-hack-security-certificates\",\n   248→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-11\",\n   249→    \"topics\": [\"OpenAI\", \"security\", \"supply chain attack\", \"ChatGPT\"],\n   250→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   251→  },\n   252→  {\n   253→    \"title\": \"Anthropic temporarily banned OpenClaw's creator from accessing Claude\",\n   254→    \"description\": \"Anthropic temporarily suspended OpenClaw's creator's access to Claude, raising questions about platform governance, API access policies, and tensions between AI platform providers and third-party tool developers.\",\n   255→    \"author\": \"Julie Bort\",\n   256→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n   257→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/11/anthropic-bans-openclaw-creator-claude-access/\",\n   258→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-11\",\n   259→    \"topics\": [\"Anthropic\", \"OpenClaw\", \"API access\", \"platform governance\", \"developer relations\"],\n   260→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   261→  },\n   262→  {\n   263→    \"title\": \"SQLite 3.53.0 release - ALTER TABLE constraints, JSON functions, and WebAssembly formatter\",\n   264→    \"description\": \"SQLite 3.53.0 is a significant release with ALTER TABLE support for adding/removing NOT NULL and CHECK constraints, new json_array_insert() function, and major CLI improvements including a new Query Results Formatter library. Simon used Claude Code on his phone to compile the formatter to WebAssembly and build a playground interface.\",\n   265→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   266→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   267→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/11/sqlite-353/\",\n   268→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-11\",\n   269→    \"topics\": [\"sql\", \"sqlite\"],\n   270→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   271→  },\n   272→  {\n   273→    \"title\": \"Claude Cowork is ready to take over your company\",\n   274→    \"description\": \"Anthropic's Claude Cowork, a shared agentic AI workspace for macOS and Windows, added IT admin tools for company-wide deployments and new features including Zoom meeting transcript-to-action-items conversion. Available for paid organizational plans.\",\n   275→    \"author\": \"Thomas Ricker\",\n   276→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n   277→    \"url\": \"https://www.theverge.com/2026/4/10/24125890/claude-cowork-it-admin-tools-zoom\",\n   278→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-10\",\n   279→    \"topics\": [\"Claude Cowork\", \"Anthropic\", \"enterprise\", \"AI agents\", \"productivity\"],\n   280→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   281→  },\n   282→  {\n   283→    \"title\": \"The growing gap in AI capability based on access points - Voice mode vs Codex\",\n   284→    \"description\": \"Simon Willison noted that OpenAI's voice mode runs on a much older, weaker model (GPT-4o era with April 2024 cutoff), while the highest-tier paid Codex model can spend hours restructuring codebases or finding vulnerabilities. This insight was inspired by Andrej Karpathy's tweet about the growing gap in understanding AI capability based on access points. The difference stems from verifiable reward functions in coding and security domains, making them more amenable to RL training.\",\n   285→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison, Andrej Karpathy\",\n   286→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   287→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/10/ai-capability-gap/\",\n   288→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-10\",\n   289→    \"topics\": [\"andrej-karpathy\", \"generative-ai\", \"openai\", \"chatgpt\", \"ai\", \"llms\"],\n   290→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n   291→  },\n   292→  {\n   293→    \"title\": \"ChatGPT has a new $100 per month Pro subscription\",\n   294→    \"description\": \"OpenAI launched a new $100/month ChatGPT Pro plan, representing a significant premium tier above existing offerings and targeting power users and businesses requiring intensive AI assistance.\",\n   295→    \"author\": \"The Verge Staff\",\n   296→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n   297→    \"url\": \"https://www.theverge.com/2026/4/9/24121450/chatgpt-pro-100-dollars-month\",\n   298→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-09\",\n   299→    \"topics\": [\"OpenAI\", \"ChatGPT\", \"pricing\", \"subscription tiers\"],\n   300→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   301→  },\n   302→  {\n   303→    \"title\": \"ChatGPT finally offers $100/month Pro plan\",\n   304→    \"description\": \"OpenAI officially launched the $100/month ChatGPT Pro plan, positioning it as a premium tier for heavy users and enterprises requiring advanced AI capabilities and higher usage limits.\",\n   305→    \"author\": \"Julie Bort\",\n   306→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n   307→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/9/openai-chatgpt-pro-100-dollar-plan/\",\n   308→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-09\",\n   309→    \"topics\": [\"OpenAI\", \"ChatGPT\", \"pricing\", \"premium tier\", \"enterprise\"],\n   310→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   311→  },\n   312→  {\n   313→    \"title\": \"Florida launches investigation into OpenAI\",\n   314→    \"description\": \"Florida Attorney General opened an investigation into OpenAI following a shooting incident that allegedly involved ChatGPT, raising new legal and regulatory scrutiny around AI safety and accountability.\",\n   315→    \"author\": \"The Verge Staff\",\n   316→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n   317→    \"url\": \"https://www.theverge.com/2026/4/9/24121340/florida-openai-investigation-shooting\",\n   318→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-09\",\n   319→    \"topics\": [\"OpenAI\", \"regulation\", \"AI safety\", \"legal issues\"],\n   320→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   321→  },\n   322→  {\n   323→    \"title\": \"The AI industry's race for profits is now existential\",\n   324→    \"description\": \"Analysis of how Anthropic and OpenAI are facing unprecedented pressure to achieve profitability, with 2026 emerging as a make-or-break year for major AI companies to demonstrate sustainable business models.\",\n   325→    \"author\": \"Nilay Patel\",\n   326→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n   327→    \"url\": \"https://www.theverge.com/2026/4/9/24120923/ai-industry-profitability-anthropic-openai\",\n   328→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-09\",\n   329→    \"topics\": [\"AI business\", \"profitability\", \"Anthropic\", \"OpenAI\", \"industry analysis\"],\n   330→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n   331→  },\n   332→  {\n   333→    \"title\": \"Is Anthropic limiting the release of Mythos to protect the internet — or Anthropic?\",\n   334→    \"description\": \"Analysis of Anthropic's cautious approach to Mythos release, exploring whether the strategy is motivated by safety concerns or competitive positioning in the AI landscape.\",\n   335→    \"author\": \"Tim Fernholz\",\n   336→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n   337→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/9/anthropic-mythos-release-strategy-safety-competition/\",\n   338→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-09\",\n   339→    \"topics\": [\"Anthropic\", \"Mythos\", \"AI safety\", \"release strategy\", \"competition\"],\n   340→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n   341→  },\n   342→  {\n   343→    \"title\": \"Sierra's Bret Taylor says the era of clicking buttons is over\",\n   344→    \"description\": \"Sierra co-founder Bret Taylor declared that traditional UI interfaces are being replaced by AI-driven conversational interfaces, signaling a fundamental shift in how users interact with software.\",\n   345→    \"author\": \"Marina Temkin\",\n   346→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n   347→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/9/sierra-bret-taylor-ai-no-more-buttons/\",\n   348→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-09\",\n   349→    \"topics\": [\"Sierra\", \"Bret Taylor\", \"conversational AI\", \"UI design\", \"software interfaces\"],\n   350→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n   351→  },\n   352→  {\n   353→    \"title\": \"PAL: Personal Adaptive Learner\",\n   354→    \"description\": \"Research paper introducing PAL, a Personal Adaptive Learner system that adapts to individual learning patterns and behaviors. Published April 15, 2026.\",\n   355→    \"author\": \"Megha Chakraborty, Darssan L. Eswaramoorthi, Madhur Thareja, et al.\",\n   356→    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n   357→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.13017\",\n   358→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-15\",\n   359→    \"topics\": [\"personalized learning\", \"adaptive AI\", \"human-computer interaction\", \"education\"],\n   360→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   361→  },\n   362→  {\n   363→    \"title\": \"Cycle-Consistent Search: Question Reconstructability as a Proxy Reward for Search Agent Training\",\n   364→    \"description\": \"Meta Superintelligence Labs researchers developed a new training method for search agents using question reconstructability as a proxy reward, improving agent performance in information retrieval tasks.\",\n   365→    \"author\": \"Sohyun An, Shuibenyang Yuan, Hayeon Lee, Cho-Jui Hsieh, Alexander Min\",\n   366→    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n   367→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.12967\",\n   368→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-15\",\n   369→    \"topics\": [\"search agents\", \"Meta\", \"reinforcement learning\", \"information retrieval\"],\n   370→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   371→  },\n   372→  {\n   373→    \"title\": \"Drawing on Memory: Dual-Trace Encoding Improves Cross-Session Recall in LLM Agents\",\n   374→    \"description\": \"Research demonstrating that dual-trace encoding significantly improves memory recall across sessions in LLM-powered agents, addressing a key challenge in maintaining context and continuity for AI assistants.\",\n   375→    \"author\": \"Benjamin Stern, Peter Nadel\",\n   376→    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n   377→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.12948\",\n   378→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-15\",\n   379→    \"topics\": [\"LLM agents\", \"memory systems\", \"cross-session recall\", \"AI architecture\"],\n   380→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   381→  },\n   382→  {\n   383→    \"title\": \"BEAM: Bi-level Memory-adaptive Algorithmic Evolution for LLM-Powered Heuristic Design\",\n   384→    \"description\": \"Introduction of BEAM, a bi-level memory-adaptive algorithm for LLM-powered heuristic design, enabling more efficient and adaptive AI systems for complex problem-solving.\",\n   385→    \"author\": \"Chuyang Xiang, Yichen Wei, Jiale Ma, et al.\",\n   386→    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n   387→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.12898\",\n   388→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-15\",\n   389→    \"topics\": [\"LLM optimization\", \"heuristic design\", \"memory systems\", \"algorithm design\"],\n   390→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   391→  },\n   392→  {\n   393→    \"title\": \"GAM: Hierarchical Graph-based Agentic Memory for LLM Agents\",\n   394→    \"description\": \"Researchers developed GAM, a hierarchical graph-based memory system for LLM agents, improving information organization and retrieval in multi-agent systems with complex reasoning requirements.\",\n   395→    \"author\": \"Zhaofen Wu, Hanrong Zhang, Fulin Lin, et al.\",\n   396→    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n   397→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.12285\",\n   398→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-15\",\n   399→    \"topics\": [\"graph memory\", \"multi-agent systems\", \"LLM agents\", \"knowledge representation\"],\n   400→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   401→  },\n   402→  {\n   403→    \"title\": \"Frontier-Eng: Benchmarking Self-Evolving Agents on Real-World Engineering Tasks\",\n   404→    \"description\": \"Introduction of Frontier-Eng, a benchmark for evaluating self-evolving AI agents on real-world engineering tasks, focusing on generative optimization and autonomous problem-solving capabilities.\",\n   405→    \"author\": \"Yizhe Chi, Deyao Hong, Dapeng Jiang, et al.\",\n   406→    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n   407→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.12290\",\n   408→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-15\",\n   409→    \"topics\": [\"self-evolving agents\", \"engineering benchmarks\", \"autonomous systems\", \"AI evaluation\"],\n   410→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   411→  },\n   412→  {\n   413→    \"title\": \"CIA: Inferring the Communication Topology from LLM-based Multi-Agent Systems\",\n   414→    \"description\": \"Research presenting CIA, a method for inferring communication topology in LLM-based multi-agent systems, helping understand and optimize how AI agents coordinate and share information.\",\n   415→    \"author\": \"Yongxuan Wu, Xixun Lin, He Zhang, et al.\",\n   416→    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n   417→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.12461\",\n   418→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-15\",\n   419→    \"topics\": [\"multi-agent systems\", \"communication topology\", \"LLM orchestration\", \"agent coordination\"],\n   420→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   421→  }\n   422→]\n   423→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
      }
