;\n   198→            font-weight: bold;\n   199→        }\n   200→\n   201→        .update-type {\n   202→            display: inline-block;\n   203→            padding: 2px 6px;\n   204→            margin-left: 5px;\n   205→            font-size: 7pt;\n   206→            background-color: #eeeeee;\n   207→            border-radius: 2px;\n   208→        }\n   209→\n   210→        @media print {\n   211→            body {\n   212→                background-color: #ffffff;\n   213→            }\n   214→\n   215→            section {\n   216→                page-break-inside: avoid;\n   217→            }\n   218→\n   219→            .three-column-layout {\n   220→                display: block;\n   221→            }\n   222→\n   223→            section {\n   224→                margin-bottom: 20px;\n   225→            }\n   226→        }\n   227→\n   228→        .stats {\n   229→            background-color: #ffffff;\n   230→            border: 1px solid #d4d4d4;\n   231→            padding: 10px;\n   232→            margin-bottom: 15px;\n   233→            font-size: 9pt;\n   234→        }\n   235→\n   236→        .stats-row {\n   237→            display: flex;\n   238→            justify-content: space-between;\n   239→            margin-bottom: 5px;\n   240→        }\n   241→\n   242→        .stats-label {\n   243→            font-weight: bold;\n   244→            color: #828282;\n   245→        }\n   246→\n   247→        .stats-value {\n   248→            color: #000000;\n   249→        }\n   250→    </style>\n   251→</head>\n   252→<body>\n   253→    <div class=\"container\">\n   254→        <header>\n   255→            <h1>Agentic Coding Research Report</h1>\n   256→            <div class=\"date\">2026-04-16</div>\n   257→        </header>\n   258→\n   259→        <div class=\"stats\">\n   260→            <div class=\"stats-row\">\n   261→                <span class=\"stats-label\">New Products & Discussions:</span>\n   262→                <span class=\"stats-value\">42 items</span>\n   263→            </div>\n   264→            <div class=\"stats-row\">\n   265→                <span class=\"stats-label\">Product Updates:</span>\n   266→                <span class=\"stats-value\">5 updates</span>\n   267→            </div>\n   268→            <div class=\"stats-row\">\n   269→                <span class=\"stats-label\">Research Insights:</span>\n   270→                <span class=\"stats-value\">0 items</span>\n   271→            </div>\n   272→        </div>\n   273→\n   274→        <main class=\"three-column-layout\">\n   275→            <section class=\"new-products\">\n   276→                <h2>New Products & Discussions</h2>\n   277→\n   278→                <div class=\"item\">\n   279→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   280→                        <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40385234\" target=\"_blank\">Show HN: Libretto – Making AI browser automations deterministic</a>\n   281→                        <span class=\"source-tag source-hn\">HN</span>\n   282→                    </div>\n   283→                    <div class=\"item-description\">A developer showcased Libretto, a tool for making AI browser automations deterministic, addressing reliability challenges in AI-powered web automation and testing workflows.</div>\n   284→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   285→                        by <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=muchael\" target=\"_blank\">muchael</a> | 2026-04-16\n   286→                    </div>\n   287→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   288→                        <span class=\"topic\">browser automation</span>\n   289→                        <span class=\"topic\">deterministic AI</span>\n   290→                        <span class=\"topic\">testing</span>\n   291→                        <span class=\"topic\">developer tools</span>\n   292→                    </div>\n   293→                </div>\n   294→\n   295→                <div class=\"item\">\n   296→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   297→                        <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40386541\" target=\"_blank\">Ask HN: Who is using OpenClaw?</a>\n   298→                        <span class=\"source-tag source-hn\">HN</span>\n   299→                    </div>\n   300→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Hacker News discussion asking about real-world adoption and use cases for OpenClaw, revealing community interest and practical applications of autonomous AI agents in development workflows.</div>\n   301→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   302→                        by <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=misterchocolat\" target=\"_blank\">misterchocolat</a> | 2026-04-16\n   303→                    </div>\n   304→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   305→                        <span class=\"topic\">OpenClaw</span>\n   306→                        <span class=\"topic\">adoption</span>\n   307→                        <span class=\"topic\">developer tools</span>\n   308→                        <span class=\"topic\">AI agents</span>\n   309→                    </div>\n   310→                </div>\n   311→\n   312→                <div class=\"item\">\n   313→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   314→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/15/gemini-flash-tts/\" target=\"_blank\">Gemini 3.1 Flash TTS - Google's new text-to-speech model</a>\n   315→                        <span class=\"source-tag source-blog\">Blog</span>\n   316→                    </div>\n   317→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Google released Gemini 3.1 Flash TTS with prompt-based voice control. Simon Willison tested it with different regional accents and noted the results.</div>\n   318→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   319→                        by <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Simon Willison</a> | 2026-04-15\n   320→                    </div>\n   321→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   322→                        <span class=\"topic\">text-to-speech</span>\n   323→                        <span class=\"topic\">google</span>\n   324→                        <span class=\"topic\">gemini</span>\n   325→                        <span class=\"topic\">prompt-engineering</span>\n   326→                    </div>\n   327→                </div>\n   328→\n   329→                <div class=\"item\">\n   330→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   331→                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/15/anthropics-rise-giving-openai-investors-second-thoughts/\" target=\"_blank\">Anthropic's rise is giving some OpenAI investors second thoughts</a>\n   332→                        <span class=\"source-tag source-techmedia\">TechMedia</span>\n   333→                    </div>\n   334→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Investment analysis suggesting Anthropic's momentum is causing OpenAI investors to reconsider their positions, highlighting growing competition in the AI space.</div>\n   335→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   336→                        by Connie Loizos | 2026-04-15\n   337→                    </div>\n   338→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   339→                        <span class=\"topic\">Anthropic</span>\n   340→                        <span class=\"topic\">OpenAI</span>\n   341→                        <span class=\"topic\">investment</span>\n   342→                        <span class=\"topic\">market competition</span>\n   343→                    </div>\n   344→                </div>\n   345→\n   346→                <div class=\"item\">\n   347→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   348→                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/15/anthropic-trump-administration-mythos-briefing/\" target=\"_blank\">Anthropic co-founder confirms Trump administration briefing on Mythos</a>\n   349→                        <span class=\"source-tag source-techmedia\">TechMedia</span>\n   350→                    </div>\n   351→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Anthropic co-founder confirmed briefing the Trump administration on Mythos, indicating growing government interest in AI capabilities and potential regulatory engagement.</div>\n   352→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   353→                        by Sarah Perez | 2026-04-15\n   354→                    </div>\n   355→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   356→                        <span class=\"topic\">Anthropic</span>\n   357→                        <span class=\"topic\">Mythos</span>\n   358→                        <span class=\"topic\">government</span>\n   359→                        <span class=\"topic\">policy</span>\n   360→                    </div>\n   361→                </div>\n   362→\n   363→                <div class=\"item\">\n   364→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   365→                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/15/google-chrome-ai-skills-feature/\" target=\"_blank\">Google adds AI Skills to Chrome to help you save favorite workflows</a>\n   366→                        <span class=\"source-tag source-techmedia\">TechMedia</span>\n   367→                    </div>\n   368→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Google introduced AI Skills in Chrome, allowing users to save AI prompts as repeatable workflows for automation of common tasks.</div>\n   369→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   370→                        by Sarah Perez | 2026-04-15\n   371→                    </div>\n   372→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   373→                        <span class=\"topic\">Google</span>\n   374→                        <span class=\"topic\">Chrome</span>\n   375→                        <span class=\"topic\">AI workflows</span>\n   376→                        <span class=\"topic\">browser automation</span>\n   377→                    </div>\n   378→                </div>\n   379→\n   380→                <div class=\"item\">\n   381→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   382→                        <a href=\"https://www.theverge.com/2026/4/14/24138473/google-gemini-mac-app\" target=\"_blank\">Google launches a Gemini AI app on Mac</a>\n   383→                        <span class=\"source-tag source-techmedia\">TechMedia</span>\n   384→                    </div>\n   385→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Google released a Gemini app for macOS, allowing users to access Gemini from anywhere on their desktop and share windows.</div>\n   386→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   387→                        by Emma Roth | 2026-04-14\n   388→                    </div>\n   389→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   390→                        <span class=\"topic\">Google Gemini</span>\n   391→                        <span class=\"topic\">macOS</span>\n   392→                        <span class=\"topic\">AI apps</span>\n   393→                        <span class=\"topic\">cross-platform</span>\n   394→                    </div>\n   395→                </div>\n   396→\n   397→                <div class=\"item\">\n   398→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   399→                        <a href=\"https://www.theverge.com/2026/4/14/24137884/adobe-firefly-conversational-ai-editing\" target=\"_blank\">Adobe embraces conversational AI editing, marking a 'fundamental shift'</a>\n   400→                        <span class=\"source-tag source-techmedia\">TechMedia</span>\n   401→                    </div>\n   402→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Adobe announced new conversational AI editing capabilities in Firefly, representing what they call a 'fundamental shift' in how creative professionals interact with AI tools.</div>\n   403→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   404→                        by Jess Weatherbed | 2026-04-14\n   405→                    </div>\n   406→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   407→                        <span class=\"topic\">Adobe</span>\n   408→                        <span class=\"topic\">conversational AI</span>\n   409→                        <span class=\"topic\">creative tools</span>\n   410→                        <span class=\"topic\">Firefly</span>\n   411→                    </div>\n   412→                </div>\n   413→\n   414→                <div class=\"item\">\n   415→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   416→                        <a href=\"https://www.theverge.com/2026/4/14/24137500/claude-code-redesign-multiple-ai-agents\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Code redesign focuses on managing multiple AI agents</a>\n   417→                        <span class=\"source-tag source-techmedia\">TechMedia</span>\n   418→                    </div>\n   419→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Anthropic redesigned the Claude Code desktop app with new features for managing multiple AI agents simultaneously, including a sidebar for managing sessions and drag-and-drop workspace customization.</div>\n   420→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   421→                        by Stevie Bonifield | 2026-04-14\n   422→                    </div>\n   423→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   424→                        <span class=\"topic\">Claude Code</span>\n   425→                        <span class=\"topic\">Anthropic</span>\n   426→                        <span class=\"topic\">multi-agent systems</span>\n   427→                        <span class=\"topic\">developer tools</span>\n   428→                    </div>\n   429→                </div>\n   430→\n   431→                <div class=\"item\">\n   432→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   433→                        <a href=\"https://www.theverge.com/2026/4/14/24137685/gemini-personal-intelligence-global-rollout\" target=\"_blank\">Gemini with Personal Intelligence is rolling out in more regions</a>\n   434→                        <span class=\"source-tag source-techmedia\">TechMedia</span>\n   435→                    </div>\n   436→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Google's Personal Intelligence feature is now rolling out globally, allowing Gemini to access information from Gmail, Google Photos, Search, and YouTube watch history.</div>\n   437→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   438→                        by Emma Roth | 2026-04-14\n   439→                    </div>\n   440→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   441→                        <span class=\"topic\">Google Gemini</span>\n   442→                        <span class=\"topic\">Personal Intelligence</span>\n   443→                        <span class=\"topic\">privacy</span>\n   444→                        <span class=\"topic\">data access</span>\n   445→                    </div>\n   446→                </div>\n   447→\n   448→                <div class=\"item\">\n   449→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   450→                        <a href=\"https://www.theverge.com/2026/4/14/24137186/microsoft-mai-image-2-efficient\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft says its latest AI image model is a 'production workhorse'</a>\n   451→                        <span class=\"source-tag source-techmedia\">TechMedia</span>\n   452→                    </div>\n   453→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Microsoft debuted MAI-Image-2-Efficient, describing it as a faster, cheaper 'production workhorse' for businesses needing volume, speed, and cost control.</div>\n   454→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   455→                        by Tom Warren | 2026-04-14\n   456→                    </div>\n   457→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   458→                        <span class=\"topic\">Microsoft</span>\n   459→                        <span class=\"topic\">AI image generation</span>\n   460→                        <span class=\"topic\">enterprise</span>\n   461→                        <span class=\"topic\">cost efficiency</span>\n   462→                    </div>\n   463→                </div>\n   464→\n   465→                <div class=\"item\">\n   466→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   467→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/14/csrf/\" target=\"_blank\">Datasette CSRF protection modernization</a>\n   468→                        <span class=\"source-tag source-blog\">Blog</span>\n   469→                    </div>\n   470→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Simon Willison landed a PR to replace Datasette's token-based CSRF protection with a modern approach using Sec-Fetch-Site headers. Notably, Claude Code did much of the work across 10 commits.</div>\n   471→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   472→                        by <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Simon Willison</a> | 2026-04-14\n   473→                    </div>\n   474→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   475→                        <span class=\"topic\">csrf</span>\n   476→                        <span class=\"topic\">security</span>\n   477→                        <span class=\"topic\">datasette</span>\n   478→                        <span class=\"topic\">ai-assisted-programming</span>\n   479→                    </div>\n   480→                </div>\n   481→\n   482→                <div class=\"item\">\n   483→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   484→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/14/openai-cyber/\" target=\"_blank\">OpenAI's GPT-5.4-Cyber model and Trusted Access program</a>\n   485→                        <span class=\"source-tag source-blog\">Blog</span>\n   486→                    </div>\n   487→                    <div class=\"item-description\">OpenAI announced GPT-5.4-Cyber, a 'cyber-permissive' variant fine-tuned for defensive cybersecurity use cases, along with their Trusted Access for Cyber program.</div>\n   488→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   489→                        by <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Simon Willison</a> | 2026-04-14\n   490→                    </div>\n   491→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   492→                        <span class=\"topic\">security</span>\n   493→                        <span class=\"topic\">ai</span>\n   494→                        <span class=\"topic\">openai</span>\n   495→                        <span class=\"topic\">anthropic</span>\n   496→                    </div>\n   497→                </div>\n   498→\n   499→                <div class=\"item\">\n   500→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   501→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/14/cyber-proof-of-work/\" target=\"_blank\">Cybersecurity as Proof of Work - The economic implications of AI security testing</a>\n   502→                        <span class=\"source-tag source-blog\">Blog</span>\n   503→                    </div>\n   504→                    <div class=\"item-description\">The UK's AI Safety Institute published an evaluation of Claude Mythos Preview's cyber capabilities. Drew Breunig notes that more tokens spent equals better security results.</div>\n   505→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   506→                        by Drew Breunig (covered by Simon Willison) | 2026-04-14\n   507→                    </div>\n   508→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   509→                        <span class=\"topic\">open-source</span>\n   510→                        <span class=\"topic\">ai</span>\n   511→                        <span class=\"topic\">generative-ai</span>\n   512→                        <span class=\"topic\">ai-security-research</span>\n   513→                    </div>\n   514→                </div>\n   515→            </section>\n   516→\n   517→            <section class=\"whitelist-updates\">\n   518→                <h2>Product Updates</h2>\n   519→\n   520→                <div class=\"item\">\n   521→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   522→                        <span class=\"product-name\">Aider</span> - Version 0.82.1 Release\n   523→                        <span class=\"update-type\">release</span>\n   524→                    </div>\n   525→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Aider released version 0.82.1 in April 2025, continuing their series of AI coding assistant updates. The repository moved from paul-gauthier/aider to Aider-AI/aider organization.</div>\n   526→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   527→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/Aider-AI/aider/releases\" target=\"_blank\">View Release</a> | 2025-04-16\n   528→                    </div>\n   529→                </div>\n   530→\n   531→                <div class=\"item\">\n   532→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   533→                        <span class=\"product-name\">Cursor</span> - Background Agents in Slack, BugBot, and Cursor 1.0\n   534→                        <span class=\"update-type\">release</span>\n   535→                    </div>\n   536→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Cursor launched version 1.0 with Background Agents in Slack integration, BugBot for automatic code review, Background Agent access for all users, Jupyter Notebook support, Memories feature, and one-click MCP setup with OAuth support.</div>\n   537→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   538→                        <a href=\"https://cursor.sh/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">View Changelog</a> | 2025-04-08\n   539→                    </div>\n   540→                </div>\n   541→\n   542→                <div class=\"item\">\n   543→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   544→                        <span class=\"product-name\">GitHub Copilot</span> - Copilot Cloud Agent and GPT-5.4 Models\n   545→                        <span class=\"update-type\">release</span>\n   546→                    </div>\n   547→                    <div class=\"item-description\">GitHub released Copilot cloud agent for research, planning, and coding, along with GPT-5.4 mini generally available, Copilot SDK in public preview, and organization custom instructions GA.</div>\n   548→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   549→                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/label/copilot/\" target=\"_blank\">View Changelog</a> | 2025-04-08\n   550→                    </div>\n   551→                </div>\n   552→\n   553→                <div class=\"item\">\n   554→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   555→                        <span class=\"product-name\">Claude Code</span> - Version 2.1.110 - TUI Mode and Push Notifications\n   556→                        <span class=\"update-type\">feature</span>\n   557→                    </div>\n   558→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Claude Code 2.1.110 added `/tui` command for flicker-free rendering, push notification tool for Remote Control, `/focus` command toggle, improved `/plugin` interface, and various performance improvements.</div>\n   559→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   560→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\" target=\"_blank\">View Changelog</a> | 2025-04-01\n   561→                    </div>\n   562→                </div>\n   563→\n   564→                <div class=\"item\">\n   565→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   566→                        <span class=\"product-name\">Windsurf</span> - Cascade AI Agent and MCP Integration\n   567→                        <span class=\"update-type\">feature</span>\n   568→                    </div>\n   569→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Windsurf features Cascade - an AI agent combining deep codebase understanding, advanced tools, and real-time awareness. Includes Windsurf Previews for live website editing, MCP integration, Tab-to-Jump navigation, Supercomplete, and Command features.</div>\n   570→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   571→                        <a href=\"https://codeium.com/windsurf\" target=\"_blank\">Learn More</a> | 2025-04-01\n   572→                    </div>\n   573→                </div>\n   574→            </section>\n   575→\n   576→            <section class=\"technical-insights\">\n   577→                <h2>Technical Insights</h2>\n   578→\n   579→                <div class=\"item\">\n   580→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   581→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.13017\" target=\"_blank\">PAL: Personal Adaptive Learner</a>\n   582→                        <span class=\"source-tag source-paper\">Paper</span>\n   583→                    </div>\n   584→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Research paper introducing PAL, a Personal Adaptive Learner system that adapts to individual learning patterns and behaviors.</div>\n   585→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   586→                        Megha Chakraborty et al. | 2026-04-15\n   587→                    </div>\n   588→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   589→                        <span class=\"topic\">personalized learning</span>\n   590→                        <span class=\"topic\">adaptive AI</span>\n   591→                    </div>\n   592→                </div>\n   593→\n   594→                <div class=\"item\">\n   595→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   596→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.12967\" target=\"_blank\">Cycle-Consistent Search: Question Reconstructability as a Proxy Reward</a>\n   597→                        <span class=\"source-tag source-paper\">Paper</span>\n   598→                    </div>\n   599→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Meta Superintelligence Labs researchers developed a new training method for search agents using question reconstructability as a proxy reward.</div>\n   600→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   601→                        Sohyun An et al. | 2026-04-15\n   602→                    </div>\n   603→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   604→                        <span class=\"topic\">search agents</span>\n   605→                        <span class=\"topic\">Meta</span>\n   606→                        <span class=\"topic\">reinforcement learning</span>\n   607→                    </div>\n   608→                </div>\n   609→\n   610→                <div class=\"item\">\n   611→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   612→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.12948\" target=\"_blank\">Drawing on Memory: Dual-Trace Encoding Improves Cross-Session Recall</a>\n   613→                        <span class=\"source-tag source-paper\">Paper</span>\n   614→                    </div>\n   615→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Research demonstrating that dual-trace encoding significantly improves memory recall across sessions in LLM-powered agents.</div>\n   616→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   617→                        Benjamin Stern, Peter Nadel | 2026-04-15\n   618→                    </div>\n   619→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   620→                        <span class=\"topic\">LLM agents</span>\n   621→                        <span class=\"topic\">memory systems</span>\n   622→                    </div>\n   623→                </div>\n   624→\n   625→                <div class=\"item\">\n   626→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   627→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.12898\" target=\"_blank\">BEAM: Bi-level Memory-adaptive Algorithmic Evolution</a>\n   628→                        <span class=\"source-tag source-paper\">Paper</span>\n   629→                    </div>\n   630→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Introduction of BEAM, a bi-level memory-adaptive algorithm for LLM-powered heuristic design.</div>\n   631→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   632→                        Chuyang Xiang et al. | 2026-04-15\n   633→                    </div>\n   634→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   635→                        <span class=\"topic\">LLM optimization</span>\n   636→                        <span class=\"topic\">heuristic design</span>\n   637→                    </div>\n   638→                </div>\n   639→\n   640→                <div class=\"item\">\n   641→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   642→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.12285\" target=\"_blank\">GAM: Hierarchical Graph-based Agentic Memory for LLM Agents</a>\n   643→                        <span class=\"source-tag source-paper\">Paper</span>\n   644→                    </div>\n   645→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Researchers developed GAM, a hierarchical graph-based memory system for LLM agents, improving information organization and retrieval in multi-agent systems.</div>\n   646→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   647→                        Zhaofen Wu et al. | 2026-04-15\n   648→                    </div>\n   649→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   650→                        <span class=\"topic\">graph memory</span>\n   651→                        <span class=\"topic\">multi-agent systems</span>\n   652→                    </div>\n   653→                </div>\n   654→\n   655→                <div class=\"item\">\n   656→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   657→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.12290\" target=\"_blank\">Frontier-Eng: Benchmarking Self-Evolving Agents</a>\n   658→                        <span class=\"source-tag source-paper\">Paper</span>\n   659→                    </div>\n   660→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Introduction of Frontier-Eng, a benchmark for evaluating self-evolving AI agents on real-world engineering tasks.</div>\n   661→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   662→                        Yizhe Chi et al. | 2026-04-15\n   663→                    </div>\n   664→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   665→                        <span class=\"topic\">self-evolving agents</span>\n   666→                        <span class=\"topic\">engineering benchmarks</span>\n   667→                    </div>\n   668→                </div>\n   669→\n   670→                <div class=\"item\">\n   671→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   672→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.12461\" target=\"_blank\">CIA: Inferring Communication Topology from Multi-Agent Systems</a>\n   673→                        <span class=\"source-tag source-paper\">Paper</span>\n   674→                    </div>\n   675→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Research presenting CIA, a method for inferring communication topology in LLM-based multi-agent systems.</div>\n   676→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   677→                        Yongxuan Wu et al. | 2026-04-15\n   678→                    </div>\n   679→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   680→                        <span class=\"topic\">multi-agent systems</span>\n   681→                        <span class=\"topic\">communication topology</span>\n   682→                    </div>\n   683→                </div>\n   684→\n   685→                <div class=\"item\">\n   686→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   687→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/13/servo-crate/\" target=\"_blank\">Exploring the new Servo crate</a>\n   688→                        <span class=\"source-tag source-blog\">Blog</span>\n   689→                    </div>\n   690→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Simon used Claude Code to explore the embeddable browser engine, building a CLI tool called 'servo-shot' for taking screenshots of URLs.</div>\n   691→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   692→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Simon Willison</a> | 2026-04-13\n   693→                    </div>\n   694→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   695→                        <span class=\"topic\">research</span>\n   696→                        <span class=\"topic\">browsers</span>\n   697→                        <span class=\"topic\">rust</span>\n   698→                        <span class=\"topic\">webassembly</span>\n   699→                    </div>\n   700→                </div>\n   701→\n   702→                <div class=\"item\">\n   703→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   704→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/13/laziness/\" target=\"_blank\">The peril of laziness lost</a>\n   705→                        <span class=\"source-tag source-blog\">Blog</span>\n   706→                    </div>\n   707→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Bryan Cantrill argues that LLMs inherently lack the virtue of laziness - work costs nothing to an LLM, so they don't optimize for future time.</div>\n   708→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   709→                        Bryan Cantrill | 2026-04-13\n   710→                    </div>\n   711→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   712→                        <span class=\"topic\">bryan-cantrill</span>\n   713→                        <span class=\"topic\">ai</span>\n   714→                        <span class=\"topic\">llms</span>\n   715→                    </div>\n   716→                </div>\n   717→\n   718→                <div class=\"item\">\n   719→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   720→                        <a href=\"https://www.theverge.com/2026/4/12/24132398/ai-code-wars-openai-google-anthropic\" target=\"_blank\">The AI code wars are heating up</a>\n   721→                        <span class=\"source-tag source-techmedia\">TechMedia</span>\n   722→                    </div>\n   723→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Analysis of how OpenAI, Google, and Anthropic are intensifying competition in AI-powered coding tools.</div>\n   724→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   725→                        by David Pierce | 2026-04-12\n   726→                    </div>\n   727→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   728→                        <span class=\"topic\">AI coding</span>\n   729→                        <span class=\"topic\">market competition</span>\n   730→                    </div>\n   731→                </div>\n   732→            </section>\n   733→        </main>\n   734→\n   735→        <footer>\n   736→            <p>Generated by <a href=\"https://agentdaily.com\" target=\"_blank\">AgentDaily</a> | Agentic Coding Research Report</p>\n   737→            <p style=\"margin-top: 5px; font-size: 8pt;\">Data sources: Hacker News, TechCrunch, The Verge, Simon Willison's Blog, arXiv</p>\n   738→        </footer>\n   739→    </div>\n   740→</body>\n   741→</html>\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
